{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1425069-azothic-channels","id":1425069,"title":"Azothic Channels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-19T18:04:02-08:00","id":1425069,"title":"Azothic Channels","content":"A while ago I wrote a story hook involving the Arisen &amp; Prometheans. It had one or more pandorans &amp; an Arisen relic &amp; was set at a museum.<br /> Certain elements of the story hook changed over time. Originally, it had an amkhat, not an Arisen relic. At one point I thought of putting in an amendment or something, saying how if you wanted you could have an amkhat &amp; a Promethean artefact be the problem, before I realized there was no such thing as Promethean artefacts. At least not officially.<br /> This is my attempt at creating a framework for some Promethean artefacts.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternate Names</b>: Flux Foci, Elpis Wands, Created Charms, Qashmallim Relics, etc.<br /> Azothic Channels, or the artefacts of Prometheans. The name Azothic Channels, being what Promethean culture is, is very informal &amp; by no means universal.<br /> How are Azothic channels created? That\u2019s a good question. There\u2019s no definite answer that says \u201cthis does the trick\u201d, however, there are a number of stories &amp; rumours on the subject. One tale says a firestorm hit a small town, when the dust cleared a number of items in the area had been transmuted into Azothic Channels. Another story claims that when a Promethean achieved New Dawn the remains of their Promethean nature spilled out onto a random object nearby. A third speaks of a qashmal dedicated to the creation production of more channels. There are others, but none are confirmed.<br /> <br /> <b>Active vs Passive</b>: active ones need to be used consciously, as in whoever wants to use one must put in a conscious effort to do so. Passive channels just work, always do so, &amp; only very rarely have off switches.<br /> <b>Standard vs Weird</b>: standard channels follow certain rules. They can rather easily be carried or moved around by a Promethean that so wishes to. They provide a set range of benefits (see below). More often than not they have extremely innocuous appearances that align with the benefits they provide. Weird channels are basically all other Azothic channels, &amp; there are no such guidelines attached to them.<br /> <b>Standard channel benefits</b>: provide the Promethean with a positive modifier regarding the use of a certain Transmutation or set of Transmutations, when filling a specific Role.<br /> <b>Weird channels effects, examples</b>: warps Torment, Disquiet, &amp;/or Wasteland; producing an ever-growing Wasteland with itself at the centre; randomly splurges out a firestorm; any human that dies a couple hours after gazing upon it, turns into a pandoran; etc.<br /> <br /> Finally if any was wondering about that story hook I mentioned at the start, here's a link to the page where I posted it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks/page6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ry-hooks/page6</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T18:56:01-08:00","id":1425075,"title":"","content":"There are Athanors (pp.188\u2013189), and there are Azothic Objects (p.111).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T19:29:33-08:00","id":1425078,"title":"","content":"Sorry I didn't see those in the book. In my defense, they don't feel like they really stand out a lot, at least from my perspective. Well, that's on Athanors.<br /> Now, Azothic Objects, supposedly on pg 111 of the same book, I just trawled through the book around that particular page &amp; found no mention of Azothic Objects.<br /> Figure it's good that there is some official objects for Promethean: The Created. After putting that first post up I realized there were some pieces missing from the framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T19:43:16-08:00","id":1425079,"title":"","content":"Sorry; p.112.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T19:50:56-08:00","id":1425080,"title":"","content":"I've got a hack somewhere on this board about an alternate take on alchemists, where a core premise is that since they can't really internalize Pyros the way Prometheans can, they instead store it in physical form as Reagents, which they can then mix together to produce the results of a Distillation that they know. I figure that technically, Prometheans can do the same thing; but they rarely bother because they don't need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T20:08:49-08:00","id":1425082,"title":"","content":"Found Azothic Objects. It would not have occurred to me to look under Merits for it, so that's why I had trouble finding that one.<br /> Despite everything that's changed, the rules on Azothic Channels above could still get some use. I'm seeing potential for my ideas on what weird Azothic Channels could be able to do be applied to Jovian Athanors.<br /> Does that sentence make sense? I think it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T23:22:43-08:00","id":1425094,"title":"","content":"It must be said that the core book shows the most common forms of Athanors.<br /> Using the same creation rules you can invent new kinds of Athanor that works in the way you have conceived for the Azothic channels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://foru